cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Economic Geography of U.S. Skill Specialization and Complexity: an interactive dashboard"
message: "If you use this dashboard, please cite both the dashboard and the underlying data release."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Howell
    given-names: Anthony
    affiliation: "School of Public Affairs, Arizona State University"
    email: ajhowel5@asu.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AntJam-Howell/skills-econ-geog-dashboard"
url: "https://antjam-howell.github.io/skills-econ-geog-dashboard/"
abstract: >-
  An open-access interactive dashboard for exploring a U.S. county-year panel
  of labor and skill demand derived from 433.6 million Lightcast (Burning
  Glass) job postings, 2010-2024. The dashboard is built on the Observable
  Framework and queries the released parquet panel client-side via DuckDB-WASM.
  Five pages cover spatial visualization, ranked tables and trends, bivariate
  county comparisons, individual county profiles, and a usage guide.
keywords:
  - economic geography
  - labor demand
  - skill demand
  - revealed comparative advantage
  - economic complexity
  - relatedness
  - Lightcast
  - job postings
  - dashboard
  - Observable Framework
